  "_about": "The closed list of reference guards an attack spec may name (meta.spec.expected[].reference). A reference is BYTES, not a name: each entry pins the wasm sha256, and tools/admission/admit.py refuses to run if the file on disk differs (checked before and after every gate run). known-good = must hold. known-bad = has exactly one documented flaw (`flaw`), so a break on it says which flaw fired. matchable=false means the guard has several differences from a known-good one, so a break on it can never be the matched positive control (it may still be listed as an extra reference). Flaw ids are a closed vocabulary: a spec's broke entry must name the same id as its reference.",
